Herve (cc'ing blavaan group),

There is currently not an automatic way to specify all residual covariances. However, you can use R's paste() function to save some typing. I would do something like this:

hsm <-  '

visual =~ x1 + x2 + x3
textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
speed =~ x7 + x8 + x9 '

rcovs <- paste(sapply(1:8, function(i) paste0("x", i, " ~~ ", paste0("x", (i+1):9, collapse=" + "))), collapse="\n")

HS.modelTOT <- paste0(hsm, "\n", rcovs)

Ed

On Tue, May 30, 2017 at 5:57 AM, Herve <herve....@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Dear Ed,
>
> thanks for the link.
>
> Question : If I want to have all residual covariances (that could be estimated with BSEM) and not cross loadings, is there a code more simple of this one :
>
> HS.modelTOT <- '

>
> visual =~ x1 + x2 + x3
> textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
> speed =~ x7 + x8 + x9

> x1  ~~ x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 + x6 + x7 + x8 + x9
> x2  ~~ x3 + x4 + x5 + x6 + x7 + x8 + x9
> x3 ~~ x4 + x5 + x6 + x7 + x8 + x9
> x4 ~~ x5 + x6 + x7 + x8 + x9
> x5 ~~ x6 + x7 + x8 + x9
> x6 ~~ x7 + x8 + x9
> x7 ~~ x8 + x9
> x8 ~~ x9
> '
> Best,
> Hervé

